 <raulalejandrooropezabatista@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 08:05:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] view: Make Copy Location put the plain path on the clipboard

Copy Location in the pathbar context menu currently copies the current
directory as a file transfer (x-special/gnome-copied-files, text/uri-list
and application/vnd.portal.filetransfer) - the same clipboard as Ctrl+C.

Apps that resolve pasted files interpret that as pasting the folder: a
Chromium-based page turns the portal file transfer into File objects and,
in a chat or agent UI, non-image files are then rejected as unsupported
image attachments ("Only PNG, JPG, WebP, and GIF images are supported"),
and messaging apps start a file upload instead of inserting the path.

Copy the absolute path as plain text instead (the URI for non-local
locations, e.g. GVFS), matching what selecting the full path in the
location entry and copying produces. Copying files and folders with
Ctrl+C is unaffected.
---
 src/nautilus-files-view.c | 22 ++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nautilus-files-view.c b/src/nautilus-files-view.c
index 17b410b..4cb967d 100644
--- a/src/nautilus-files-view.c
+++ b/src/nautilus-files-view.c
@@ -5929,18 +5929,24 @@ action_copy_current_location (GSimpleAction *action,
                               gpointer       user_data)
 {
     NautilusFilesView *self = user_data;
+    GFile *location;
+    g_autofree char *text = NULL;
     GdkClipboard *clipboard;
-    GList *files;
 
-    if (self->directory_as_file != NULL)
+    location = nautilus_files_view_get_location (self);
+    if (location == NULL)
     {
-        files = g_list_append (NULL, nautilus_file_ref (self->directory_as_file));
-
-        clipboard = gtk_widget_get_clipboard (GTK_WIDGET (self));
-        nautilus_clipboard_prepare_for_files (clipboard, files, FALSE);
-
-        nautilus_file_list_free (files);
+        return;
     }
+
+    text = g_file_get_path (location);
+    if (text == NULL)
+    {
+        text = g_file_get_uri (location);
+    }
+
+    clipboard = gtk_widget_get_clipboard (GTK_WIDGET (self));
+    gdk_clipboard_set_text (clipboard, text);
 }
 
 static void
